hey so I'm learning C from an old book and I typed in this example and it compiles but sometimes it prints garbage or crashes, my friend said something about a buffer overflow but I don't really get it. here's the code:

```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <string.h>

int main(void) {
    char name[8];
    strcpy(name, "Alexandria");
    printf("Hello, %s\n", name);
    return 0;
}
```

can you fix it so it's safe? I'd like to still use a fixed-size array if possible

