original:
ok so I have this function that finds duplicate values in an array and it works fine on small test data but when we run it on the real data which is like 200k items the page freezes for ages. I'm pretty sure it's the nested loops. here it is:

```js
function findDuplicates(arr) {
  const dups = [];
  for (let i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {
    for (let j = i + 1; j < arr.length; j++) {
      if (arr[i] === arr[j] && !dups.includes(arr[i])) {
        dups.push(arr[i]);
      }
    }
  }
  return dups;
}
```

can you make it faster, ideally O(n)? the output order doesn't matter

